{"strongs": "H3196", "word": "יַ֫יִן", "translit": "ya.yin", "root": "יין", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "wine", "definition": "יַ֫יִן 141 noun masculine Ps 75:9 wine (Late Hebrew id. ; Ethiopic : vitis, vinea, vinum ; Arabic ( black ) grapes , see Hom ZMG 1889, 654 ; Sabean וין vineyard , Mordt ZMG 1887, 364 Hom l.c. 659 (both after Glaser); Assyrian inu in vocabularies, but this loan-word from western Shemites, according to Hom Aufsätze 102 ; Jen ZA i, 186 f., ZMG 1890, 705 argues to the contrary) — absolute יַ֫יִן Gen 9:21 + 84 t.; יָ֑יִן Gen 14:18 + 33 t.; construct יַ֫יִן Ps 60:5 ; Song 8:2 יֵין Deut 32:18 + 9 t.; suffix יֵינִי Song 5:1 , etc.; — wine: \\ \\ a. common drink, for refreshment Gen 14:18 (E?) Gen 27:25 ( J ), Judg 19:19 ; 2Sam 16:2 ; Amos 5:11 ; Amos 9:14 ; Hos 14:8 ; Job 1:13 ; Job 1:18 ; Dan 1:5 +, tonic Prov 31:6 article of commerce Ezek 27:18 ; Neh 13:15 among supplies in strongholds 2Chr 11:11 as making merry 2Sam 13:28 ; Zech 9:15 ; Zech 10:7 ; Esth 1:10 ; Eccl 9:7 ; Eccl 10:19 ; Ps 104:15 . \\ \\ b. used for rejoicing before ׳ י Deut 14:26 , compare Hos 9:4 as drink-offering in prescribed ritual Exod 29:40 ; Lev 23:13 ; Num 15:5 ; Num 15:7 ; Num 15:10 ; Num 28:14 among temple stores 1Chr 9:29 used also in heathen ceremonial, see Deut 32:33 . \\ \\ c. intoxicating 1Sam 1:14 ; 1Sam 25:37 ; Gen 9:21 ; Gen 9:24 ; Gen 19:32 ; Gen 19:33 ; Gen 19:34 ; Gen 19:35 (all J ), Isa 5:11 ; Isa 5:22 ; Prov 21:17 ; Prov 23:30 ; Prov 23:31 +; || תִּירוֺשׁ Hos 4:11 || שֵׁכָר 1Sam 1:15 ; Mic 2:11 ; Isa 24:9 ; Isa 28:7 (twice in verse); Isa 56:12 + 12 t.; forbidden to Nazirites Num 6:3 (twice in verse) ( חֹמֶץ יַיִן וְחֹמֶץ שֵׁכָר ), v Num 6:4 v Num 6:20 , compare Amos 2:12 to Rechabites Jer 35:2 ; Jer 35:5 f.; to mother of Samson Judg 13:4 ; Judg 13:7 ; Judg 13:14 to priests entering sanctuary Lev 10:9 ( P ), Ezek 44:21 unfitting for kings Prov 31:4 . \\ \\ d. combinations are: יֵין הַטּוֺב Song 7:10 = the best wine (read כַּיַּיִן ?) Ges «GKC:133»§ 133 . 3, R. 1; יֵין מַלְכוּת Esth 1:7 royal wine ; אֹצרְוֺת יַּיִן 1Chr 27:27 stores of wine, wine-supply ; יַיִן הָרֶקַח Song 8:2 spiced wine ; מִשְׁתֵּה הַיַּיִן wine-feast Esth 5:6 ; Esth 7:2 ; Esth 7:7 ; Esth 7:8 סֹבְאֵי יַיִן Prov 23:20 wine-bibbers ; נאֹד יין wine-skin Josh 9:4 ; Josh 9:13 ; 1Sam 16:20 נֵבֶל יין id. 1Sam 1:24 ; 1Sam 10:3 ; 1Sam 25:18 ; 2Sam 16:1 ; Jer 13:12 (twice in verse); בֵּית הַיָּ֑יִן Song 2:4 either wine-house , where wine is drunk, feasting-house ( De and others), or place of wine = vineyard ( Ew and others; compare גֶּפֶן יַיִן Num 6:4 ). \\ \\ e. metaphor of wisdom's drink Prov 9:2 ; Prov 9:5 , compare Isa 55:1 of ׳ י 's wrath Jer 25:15 ( כּוֺס היין ); of confusion sent by ׳ י , יַיִן תַּרְעֵלָה wine of reeling Ps 60:5 , compare Ps 75:9 of ׳ י 's awaking for vengeance, like a wine-shouter Ps 78:65 of Babylon's fierce power Jer 51:7 of love Song 5:1 יֵין חֲמָסִים Prov 4:17 in simile of one bursting with words Job 32:19 of disheartened prophet Jer 23:9 ( כְּגֶבֶר עֲבָרוֺיַיִן ); of lover's mouth Song 7:10 (see above); love is better than wine Song 1:2 ; Song 4:10 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3534')\">BDB3534</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3196')\">H3196</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3533')\">BDB3533</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3535')\">BDB3535</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>יַ֫יִן</bdbheb><sub>141</sub> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Ps 75:9\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"75\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"75\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(19,75,9)\">Ps 75:9</ref></sup> <highlightword>wine</highlightword> (Late Hebrew <highlight>id.</highlight>; Ethiopic <placeholder2218/>: <highlight>vitis, vinea, vinum</highlight>; Arabic <placeholder2219/> (<highlight>black</highlight>) <highlight>grapes</highlight>, see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Hom')\">Hom<sup>ZMG 1889, 654</sup></lookup>; Sabean <bdbheb>וין</bdbheb> <highlight>vineyard</highlight>, Mordt<sup>ZMG 1887, 364